**Verdict**: `change_requested` (REQUEST_CHANGES posted)

**Finding**: One 🔴 blocker in `src/features/workspaces/context/WorkspaceContext.tsx` — the `closeTaskTab` function's `setActiveSurface` updater unconditionally returns `"board"` whenever the surface is `"task-tab"`, even when the tab being closed is not the active tab. With two or more task tabs open, closing a non-active tab incorrectly navigates the user to the board instead of keeping them on the active task tab.

**Fix required**:
```typescript
const closeTaskTab = useCallback((taskId: string) => {
  setOpenTaskTabs((prev) => prev.filter((t) => t.taskId !== taskId));
  if (activeTaskTabId === taskId) {
    setActiveTaskTabId(null);
    setActiveSurface("board");
  }
}, [activeTaskTabId]);
```

Three 🟢 nits were also noted (deprecated `execCommand` fallback, `openTaskTab` title update skip, and back-to-feature-tab deferred to T5), none of which block merge.

**Result written** to `/tmp/reviewer-result-T4.json` with `terminal_status: "change_requested"`, confidence 0.87.

